    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **56 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nThe codebase already had an established pattern for derived owner fields (`locality`): a getter on the `Owner` entity plus a `readOnly` field in `openapi.yml`, which generates `OwnerDto` and is wired by MapStruct's name-based mapping. I followed that exact pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `getTimezone()` method that resolves the IANA name from `getLocality()`, returning `null` for regions not in the table (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` `readOnly` string field to the owner schema so the generated DTO carries it, letting MapStruct auto-map `getTimezone()` \u2192 `setTimezone()`.\n\nThe new `Cp42Tests` and all 56 existing tests are green.",
